ng. So while you may not notice any hot or cold spots room-to-room, your body is still subject to the physics of radiant exchange and evaporation. That’s why a uniformly 72°F house can still feel drafty and chilly in winter but perfectly pleasant in summer, even if every room feels “the same” within each season. The environment’s relationship to your body changes seasonally, even if the thermostat doesn’t.
